<%- await include('_nav') %>
<%- await include('_cbtabs') %>

<% if (note === 'saved') { %><div class="note ok" style="margin-bottom:14px">The train is on the list.</div><% } %>
<% if (note === 'removed') { %><div class="note" style="margin-bottom:14px">Taken off the sheet. Calls already recorded against it are untouched.</div><% } %>
<% if (note === 'default') { %><div class="note ok" style="margin-bottom:14px">Saved. This is the tab the call sheet will open on here.</div><% } %>

<div class="note" style="margin-bottom:16px">
  This is the list the daily sheet is built from — the running room's own copy of what the control office
  holds in its loco link. Nothing here is a call; it is what to expect. Rows marked <b>imported</b> came from
  <code>node db/import-call-sheet.js</code> and are refreshed when it is run again; rows you edit here are
  marked <b>by hand</b> and the import will not overwrite them.
  <br><br>
  <b>Direction matters and is easy to get backwards.</b> A crew works down to Igatpuri, is relieved, sleeps,
  and is called for an <b>UP</b> train back towards Mumbai — so Igatpuri's sheet is the UP trains. When the
  neighbouring divisions come on this stops being the whole story: Bhusawal's crews rest at Igatpuri too and
  are called for <b>DN</b> trains onward. A room that serves both carries both, and the import can be run
  with <code>--direction BOTH</code>.
</div>

<div class="grid" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-h"><h3><%= rr.name %> — <%= fmtInt(trains.filter(t => t.is_active).length) %> trains</h3>
      <span class="sub">ordered as the sheet orders them</span></div>
    <div class="tblwrap"><table class="tbl">
      <thead><tr><th style="width:64px">Sign on</th><th style="width:150px">Train</th><th style="width:56px">Dir</th>
        <th style="width:62px">Sheet</th>
        <th style="width:110px">Runs</th><th style="width:74px">Train due</th><th>Where from</th>
        <th style="width:90px">Source</th><th style="width:70px"></th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      <% trains.forEach(function(t){ %>
        <tr<%= t.is_active ? '' : ' style="opacity:.45"' %>>
          <td class="tnum"><%= t.sign_on_time || '—' %></td>
          <td class="tnum"><b><%= t.train_no %></b>
            <% if (t.train_name) { %><div class="muted" style="font-size:10.5px"><%= t.train_name %></div><% } %></td>
          <td><span class="pill" style="font-size:9.5px"><%= t.direction %></span></td>
          <td><span class="pill" style="font-size:9px"><%= (t.service || 'mail').toUpperCase() %></span></td>
          <td style="font-size:12px"><%= t.run_days %></td>
          <td class="tnum"><%= t.arrives_at || '—' %></td>
          <td style="font-size:12px"><%= [t.from_station, t.to_station].filter(Boolean).join(' → ') || '—' %>
            <% if (t.notes) { %><div class="muted" style="font-size:10.5px"><%= t.notes %></div><% } %></td>
          <td><span class="st <%= t.source === 'imported' ? '' : 'good' %>" style="font-size:10px">
            <span class="dot"></span><%= t.source === 'imported' ? 'imported' : t.source === 'learned' ? 'learned' : 'by hand' %></span>
            <% if (!t.is_active) { %><div class="muted" style="font-size:10px">off the sheet</div><% } %></td>
          <td>
            <% if (t.is_active) { %>
              <form method="post" action="<%= url('/records/call-sheet-trains') %>">
                <input type="hidden" name="rr" value="<%= rr.id %>">
                <button class="btn ghost" type="submit" name="remove" value="<%= t.id %>"
                        style="font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 7px">Remove</button>
              </form>
            <% } %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% }); %>
      <% if (!trains.length) { %>
        <tr><td colspan="9" class="muted">
          Nothing on the list yet. Seed it with <code>node db/import-call-sheet.js</code>, or add trains here
          one at a time.</td></tr>
      <% } %>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-h"><h3>Add or correct a train</h3>
      <span class="sub">saving an existing number corrects it</span></div>
    <div class="card-b">
      <form method="post" action="<%= url('/records/call-sheet-trains') %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="rr" value="<%= rr.id %>">
        <div class="row" style="gap:8px;margin-bottom:10px">
          <div style="flex:1"><label class="fl">Train number</label>
            <input class="fi" name="train_no" maxlength="12" required placeholder="12072"></div>
          <div style="flex:0 0 92px"><label class="fl">Direction</label>
            <select class="fi" name="direction">
              <option value="UP">UP</option><option value="DN">DN</option>
              <option value="BYPASS">BYPASS</option><option value="OTHER">Other</option>
            </select></div>
          <div style="flex:0 0 96px"><label class="fl">Sheet</label>
            <select class="fi" name="service">
              <option value="mail">Mail</option><option value="goods">Goods</option>
            </select></div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:10px"><label class="fl">Name <span class="muted">— if it has one</span></label>
          <input class="fi" name="train_name" maxlength="120" placeholder="Jan Shatabdi"></div>
        <div class="row" style="gap:8px;margin-bottom:10px">
          <div style="flex:1"><label class="fl">Sign on at</label>
            <input class="fi" type="time" name="sign_on_time"></div>
          <div style="flex:1"><label class="fl">Runs on</label>
            <input class="fi" name="run_days" value="DAILY" maxlength="20"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="muted" style="font-size:11px;margin-bottom:10px">
          <b>DAILY</b>, or days as numbers separated by commas — <b>1 is Monday, 7 is Sunday</b>. So a train
          running Monday, Wednesday and Friday is <code>1,3,5</code>. That is the control office sheet's own
          convention, so somebody reading both sees one thing.
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:12px"><label class="fl">Note</label>
          <input class="fi" name="notes" maxlength="200" placeholder="goods link, seasonal, etc."></div>
        <button class="btn" type="submit">Put it on the sheet</button>
      </form>
      <div class="hr"></div>
      <form method="post" action="<%= url('/records/call-sheet-trains') %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="rr" value="<%= rr.id %>">
        <label class="fl">Which tab this running room opens on</label>
        <select class="fi" name="set_default" style="margin-bottom:8px" onchange="this.form.submit()">
          <option value="mail"  <%= rr.call_sheet_default === 'goods' ? '' : 'selected' %>>Mail / Express</option>
          <option value="goods" <%= rr.call_sheet_default === 'goods' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Goods</option>
        </select>
        <noscript><button class="btn ghost" type="submit" style="font-size:11.5px">Save</button></noscript>
        <div class="muted" style="font-size:11px;margin-bottom:10px">
          A goods-only running room is marked once and its bearer never clicks again. The other tab stays
          reachable either way — the day something unusual happens must not be the day the register cannot
          hold it.
        </div>
      </form>
      <div class="hr"></div>
      <div class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px">
        Keeping this list is the Railway's business, not the contractor's. A contractor who could edit which
        trains are expected could edit away the evidence that one was never called — so the contractor's
        supervisor works the daily sheet and cannot open this page.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
